    "clue_custom_text1": "There's exactly one outlaw hiding amongst the suspects. The outlaw may or may not be the murderer.",
    "clue_custom_text2": "The outlaw was beside a table.",
    "clothes_theme": "classic",
    "player_hint_count": "7",
    "player_hint_1_en": "According to the clues, the outlaw must be a suspect who's beside a table, and with (H), who's sitting in a chair. (H) would block all squares beside a table if she was sitting in R2 C1 or R9 C2. And no suspect could possibly be an outlaw and fit beside the table in the Chapel.",
    "player_hint_2_en": "So, the only area where (H) could possibly sit with a suspect who's beside a table is in the Bank. By placing (H) on the R7 C10 chair, (E) is the only suspect who can fit in any square beside a table in the Bank. Block (E)'s intersecting square, R10 C9.",
    "player_hint_3_en": "This isolates (A) in the last square beside a Register. (I) is south of (H), so (I) and (E) must be in R8 and R10, in any order. No one else can fit in these two rows.",
    "player_hint_4_en": "This isolates (F) on the last horse, then (E). This sets (I) in R8.",
    "player_hint_5_en": "(G) is in R5 C2 or R6 C5, block the intersecting squares R6 C2 and R5 C5. This isolates (C) in the last chair.",
    "player_hint_6_en": "(B) is in R6 C3 or R1 C5, block the intersecting squares R6 C5 and R1 C3. This isolates (G) in the last square beside a cactus.",
    "player_hint_7_en": "This isolates (D) in the last square beside a chair, then (I) in the last R8 square, then (B) in the last corner, then (V) in the last square."
  },
